      "message": "In this case, the app needn\u0027t to known what interface the service was discovered on, but it needs an right IP address.\n\nWhithout this change, the app can discover two different services from different network (i.e., the device use two interface connect to different network) with same hostname. After two services be resolved, thay will use same hostname to get the IP address, the IP address must be wrong for one of them. If the interface is specified, two services will all get right IP address.\n\nBecause service resolve and get IP address is combined into NsdManager#resolveService, so this change isn\u0027t aware for the user app.\n \nWhen the app gets the right IP address, it can connect to service by IP address. (The app doesn\u0027t care what interface be used to connect service. That is the job of the routing.)\n\nThe above is my opinion, please correct me. Thanks.",
